WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.025
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:08.711
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.011 --> 00:00:16.749
Unit twenty-four: City Environmental Problems. Today you will explain causes and effects with because and so.

4
00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:19.667
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.601
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.358
Pollution.

7
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.721
Pollution means dirty air, water or land.

8
00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:31.351
Air pollution makes people cough.

9
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.579
Your turn. Say: Pollution.

10
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:38.342
Pollution.

11
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:40.003
Traffic.

12
00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:43.666
Traffic means cars and motorbikes on the road.

13
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.598
The traffic is terrible at five o'clock.

14
00:00:47.183 --> 00:00:49.569
Your turn. Say: Traffic.

15
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:53.249
Traffic.

16
00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:54.833
Waste.

17
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.418
Waste means rubbish that people throw away.

18
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.063
Plastic waste blocks the drains.

19
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.000
Your turn. Say: Waste.

20
00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:07.810
Waste.

21
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.400
Noise.

22
00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:12.927
Noise means loud, unpleasant sound.

23
00:01:13.517 --> 00:01:15.447
Construction noise wakes me up.

24
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.226
Your turn. Say: Noise.

25
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.126
Noise.

26
00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:24.175
Air quality.

27
00:01:25.183 --> 00:01:28.286
Air quality means how clean or dirty the air is.

28
00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:30.918
The air quality is poor today.

29
00:01:31.517 --> 00:01:34.320
Your turn. Say: Air quality.

30
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.400
Air quality.

31
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.523
Green space.

32
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:44.921
Green space means a park or area with grass and trees.

33
00:01:45.517 --> 00:01:47.830
Our city needs more green space.

34
00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:51.638
Your turn. Say: Green space.

35
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.989
Green space.

36
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.774
Solution.

37
00:01:58.783 --> 00:02:01.236
Solution means a way to solve a problem.

38
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.675
Public buses are one solution.

39
00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:06.820
Your turn. Say: Solution.

40
00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:10.645
Solution.

41
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:12.187
City.

42
00:02:13.183 --> 00:02:15.276
City means a large, busy town.

43
00:02:15.883 --> 00:02:17.813
Phnom Penh is a growing city.

44
00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:20.732
Your turn. Say: City.

45
00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:24.394
City.

46
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.967
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:33.488
Visal, what environmental problem affects your city most?

48
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:38.687
Traffic. There is heavy traffic, so the air is polluted.

49
00:02:39.783 --> 00:02:41.458
Why is there so much traffic?

50
00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:45.351
Because many people use motorbikes and cars.

51
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.707
What's a solution?

52
00:02:48.817 --> 00:02:55.161
More buses and green space. Trees clean the air, so the air quality improves.

53
00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.719
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:58.583 --> 00:03:02.197
Grammar focus: Cause and effect (because and so).

55
00:03:02.497 --> 00:03:03.707
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:07.113
There is heavy traffic, so the air is polluted.

57
00:03:08.017 --> 00:03:10.713
The air is polluted because there is heavy traffic.

58
00:03:11.617 --> 00:03:14.545
Trees clean the air, so the city is healthier.

59
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.139
'Because' introduces the reason. 'So' introduces the result.

60
00:03:19.883 --> 00:03:24.742
Be careful! Don't say: There is heavy traffic, because the air is polluted.

61
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.081
Say: There is heavy traffic, so the air is polluted.

62
00:03:30.381 --> 00:03:33.042
Use 'so' for the result and 'because' for the reason.

63
00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:36.300
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.728
Problems and Solutions.

65
00:03:39.028 --> 00:03:41.562
Many cities have environmental problems.

66
00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:46.029
There is a lot of traffic, so there is pollution and noise.

67
00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:50.298
Waste builds up because people throw rubbish in the street.

68
00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.915
Planting green space improves air quality.

69
00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.467
If we work together, we can find a solution for our city.

70
00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:04.068
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:04.917 --> 00:04:07.508
There is heavy traffic, blank the air is polluted.

72
00:04:07.808 --> 00:04:11.276
A, so. B, because. C, but.

73
00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:16.903
The answer is A: so.

74
00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.967
A park or area with grass and trees is blank.

75
00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:25.338
A, green space. B, waste. C, traffic.

76
00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.225
The answer is A: green space.

77
00:04:32.383 --> 00:04:34.615
Loud, unpleasant sound is blank.

78
00:04:34.915 --> 00:04:38.557
A, noise. B, pollution. C, air quality.

79
00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.158
The answer is A: noise.

80
00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:48.762
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:49.617 --> 00:04:52.951
What environmental problem affects your city most?

82
00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.250
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:12.646
Waste is the biggest problem in my city. People throw plastic in the street, so the drains get blocked and the streets flood.

84
00:05:12.946 --> 00:05:14.667
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:15.583 --> 00:05:20.430
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and cause and effect (because and so).

86
00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:25.971
Today's value is civic responsibility. Take care of your city, because it is everyone's home.

87
00:05:26.271 --> 00:05:29.191
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

88
00:05:29.491 --> 00:05:32.131
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

